 Training follows a curriculum that progresses from basic goal reaching and single-obstacle avoidance to randomized clutter and moving-obstacle scenarios. The current mixed curriculum assigns approximately 55\% of episodes to complex static scenes, 35\% to basic navigation tasks, and 10\% to dynamic-obstacle scenes. In the planned integrated system, SLAM will provide a corrected robot pose for computing the relative waypoint given to the PPO policy, allowing the robot to perform local waypoint-to-waypoint navigation while mapping continues online. The next stage is to transfer this policy to the physical MentorPi and reduce sim-to-real differences in LiDAR sensing, robot motion, and control latency.
 
